    "text": "Certainly! Below is the implementation of the lambda-based function `unique` written in Python:\n\n```python\n\ndef unique(lst: list):\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique elements in a list\n    >>> unique([5, 3, 5, 2, 3, 3, 9, 0, 123])\n    [0, 2, 3, 5, 9, 123]\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_elements = list(set(lst))\n    return sorted(unique_elements)\n\n# Example usage\nif __ __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import doctest\n    doctest.testmod()\n```\n\nThis lambda function uses the `set` to remove duplicates from the input list to then convert it back to a sorted list. The `sorted` lambda function is used to sort the list in ascending order.",
